{
  "assumption_links": [],
  "authority_effect": "none",
  "correspondence": [
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-1",
      "end_character": 265,
      "excerpt": "Provenance is not proof, not authority, not trust, not validation, and not\ncredit assignment by itself. A perfect source trail can still point to a false,\nunpromoted, private, or unusable claim. It only tells the project where meaning\nand transformations came from.",
      "unit_id": "unit-a65ee39198def77dae32b1c1e1838c68d5a51b538c7f36c7344948b9db08dfb9"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-2",
      "end_character": 251,
      "excerpt": "Candidate Definition reconstructed from an accepted normalization scaffold and exact CyberAlchemy-v2 source sections. It is not admitted and grants no implementation, migration, registry, publication, release, deployment, or external-effect authority.",
      "unit_id": "unit-551051d584e8331e5ddcc495261d314ed89f7cf4cc2e9b5d89d0ceba64f24fbe"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-3",
      "end_character": 226,
      "excerpt": "Use provenance before promoting, adapting, importing, validating, or publishing\nanything. Provenance answers what source material is being used, what happened\nto it, and where the current object should be audited if it drifts.",
      "unit_id": "unit-f38b3478d5f5f0f807c00c44291d0ca3448bc7a4de1fb2aed5443376ef37ce77"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-4",
      "end_character": 13,
      "excerpt": "scope.lineage",
      "unit_id": "unit-501da9fd1d3ff66fda490fe8b836bb3811abb6634fe14a31167b453d82c5a0b6"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-5",
      "end_character": 78,
      "excerpt": "Admission, activation, publication, release, deployment, and external effects.",
      "unit_id": "unit-8dec732fb5d927545d4bf5c1bea73405d34e388983cdba3240a36b63ba348803"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-6",
      "end_character": 88,
      "excerpt": "Meanings assigned to split or reclassified sibling targets unless explicitly referenced.",
      "unit_id": "unit-94bf2030418c421474ce1629a5f3255fde290758d03623f29467345f93ee9ea0"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-7",
      "end_character": 83,
      "excerpt": "Resolve semantic.provenance by its machine identity rather than its directory name.",
      "unit_id": "unit-64b7bef41c119922ebfcfcabad834a929b2c6fabdcd395ee3534638019fd0cab"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-8",
      "end_character": 79,
      "excerpt": "Challenge source drift through the L1 drift audit before relying on Provenance.",
      "unit_id": "unit-869b0516bc21bde2cd72bf0ef9e47b73b4882152c0e789cac4629a685a802c0d"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-9",
      "end_character": 600,
      "excerpt": "In CyberAlchemy-lab migration work, Provenance is a prototype meaning reconstructed from CAL-NORMALIZE-01. It remains non-authoritative until the correct Lab owner admits a fully validated candidate.\n\nSource context retained for reconstruction:\n\nIn CyberAlchemy v2, provenance is the lower-level basis for\n`CAV2-D24` provenance-first navigation, authority imports, source clusters,\ninventory evidence cards, Craft links, handoffs, and future extraction review.\nIt lets v2 import scattered work without flattening source ownership or\npretending that source evidence has already become local authority.",
      "unit_id": "unit-e809cfc14283b35cd1eb1e8ee69e0e445e4554e0174538460dc0b93e5dad1bad"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-10",
      "end_character": 41,
      "excerpt": "/home/vrondelli/projects/CyberAlchemy-lab",
      "unit_id": "unit-ffa309e64b53ab85866dd9c0bce78b5cb2d9a40913e906c9ea92bc3faa5b2ed5"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-11",
      "end_character": 82,
      "excerpt": "Provenance is the receipt trail for where something came from and how it got\nhere.",
      "unit_id": "unit-af673a174f72eea4d6dd86549a55481a62ac2fce2724716fb66cbe88b2c17540"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-12",
      "end_character": 265,
      "excerpt": "Provenance is not proof, not authority, not trust, not validation, and not\ncredit assignment by itself. A perfect source trail can still point to a false,\nunpromoted, private, or unusable claim. It only tells the project where meaning\nand transformations came from.",
      "unit_id": "unit-268996b041b159a42c2b4ca7daeaa1ba0fb1de3f6bd996af4b2585298bbf0a57"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-13",
      "end_character": 310,
      "excerpt": "For object `x`, provenance is a typed path:\n\n```text\nProv(x) = [(source_i, relation_i, operation_i, owner_i, posture_i)]*\n```\n\nThe path may be incomplete only if the missing segment is explicitly recorded\nas residue with an owner route. Untyped \"came from\" language is not sufficient\nfor authority-bearing use.",
      "unit_id": "unit-a4250dc0e4df6d358f22e004aea4f9e66c91fc4ebd8dae8a28d53b52e92e8766"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-14",
      "end_character": 915,
      "excerpt": "Provenance is the normalized definition identified by semantic.provenance, owned within scope.lineage, and carried by type.definition. Any canonical instance must preserve that classification and the accepted source relations to CAV2-D35 without silently merging it with another target.\n\nBound source-semantic basis:\n\nProvenance is the declared origin and transformation chain for a term, artifact,\nclaim, rule, decision, relation, validation result, or residue. It records where\nthe object came from, which sources or prior objects it depends on, which\noperations changed it, which owners or processes handled it, and which\nauthority posture it held at each relevant step.\n\nProvenance must identify source references and relation types with enough\nprecision that a later reviewer can distinguish source evidence, local\nadaptation, promotion, demotion, translation, derivation, validation, and\ngenerated projection.",
      "unit_id": "unit-c52a77a6d90141f128444e561d51062f05ac5b8760d872fe573e966a78869a5d"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-15",
      "end_character": 42,
      "excerpt": "Stable normalized identity for Provenance.",
      "unit_id": "unit-40def8d9c70bdb7920cde1a1725ed8600f6359a887d7d6758750f2e17e4ff0e5"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-16",
      "end_character": 19,
      "excerpt": "semantic.provenance",
      "unit_id": "unit-0b14efa9c0a47c8e64800e710863327aae5071ec505fc474b74f413d9ee50f07"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-17",
      "end_character": 49,
      "excerpt": "Bound CyberAlchemy-v2 source-definition identity.",
      "unit_id": "unit-589257840cd95cd1a238672e86bd6b9137eba67d8ce5929322ef98c2127693fd"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-18",
      "end_character": 8,
      "excerpt": "CAV2-D35",
      "unit_id": "unit-bf52f08e60bcfff13f3763d681f6afdddf70f4516acd3f4898c9b024c175f48a"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-19",
      "end_character": 57,
      "excerpt": "The candidate identity remains cal.definition.provenance.",
      "unit_id": "unit-cd1c810b71930fdecdf8a061b7eff47ebf827864b62f1f8e85fbc27f99535e85"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-20",
      "end_character": 53,
      "excerpt": "Every selected source-section digest remains current.",
      "unit_id": "unit-62d9b9f0f2e14b44077e3a0db7904079fca058376b549a92223861c2220f97bc"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-21",
      "end_character": 51,
      "excerpt": "The machine record validates against Definition/v1.",
      "unit_id": "unit-6e0a36a3e7ce10e3274f2fe9e2ee41f7701f2c203d126d1278b94a5f3bd6b8fd"
    },
    {
      "clause_id": "clause-22",
      "end_character": 68,
      "excerpt": "The human projection is regenerated exactly from the machine record.",
      "unit_id": "unit-6e3477ec8786dca6eee728124933d1959d2501d9fa6c5a4a317baaec6d87d593"
    }
  ],
